+# Enterprise hardening & peer-parity upgrade — 2026-08-01
+
+Goal: close the highest-impact gaps between Auricrux App and the flagship assistants
+(ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Copilot, Grok) and harden the service to an enterprise posture.
+Every change below ships with tests; the suite went from 57 to 77+ passing tests.
+
+## 1. Streaming responses (SSE) — peer-parity gap closed
+
+Every major assistant streams tokens; Auricrux previously buffered the entire completion.
+
+- `POST /api/chat/stream` emits `data:` server-sent events — content deltas as the model
+  generates them, then a terminal `done=true` event carrying the full `ChatResponse`
+  (sources, interaction id, timing). Same freemium/entitlement gating as `/api/chat`.
+- Ollama is now called with `stream: true` (NDJSON parsing) on this path; corpus fallback
+  still streams when no model is reachable.
+- `AuricruxApiClient.SendChatStreamAsync` + `AuricruxService.ProcessQueryStreamAsync`
+  consume the stream; the Blazor chat page renders the assistant bubble incrementally with
+  a one-shot non-streaming retry on transport failure.
+
+## 2. Cloud frontier-model connectors — peer-parity gap closed
+
+Local Ollama remains the default runtime; the app can now also route to hosted frontier
+models when (and only when) API keys are configured. No key, no provider — nothing is
+hardcoded and nothing dials out by default.
+
+- `CloudModelGateway` supports **OpenAI**, **Anthropic (Claude)**, **Google Gemini**,
+  **xAI (Grok)**, and **Azure OpenAI** using raw HTTPS (no SDK dependencies), including
+  SSE streaming for all five.
+- Model names are provider-prefixed: `openai:gpt-4o-mini`, `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-5`,
+  `gemini:gemini-2.0-flash`, `xai:grok-3`, `azure:<deployment>`. Unprefixed names route to
+  Ollama exactly as before.
+- Keys resolve from `Auricrux:Providers:{Name}:ApiKey` or conventional env vars
+  (`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`/`GOOGLE_API_KEY`, `XAI_API_KEY`,
+  `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY` + `AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT`). `GET /api/models` lists cloud models
+  only for providers with a resolvable key.
+
+## 3. Deny-by-default API authorization — security gap closed
+
+Previously only `/api/secure/ping` honored `Auth:Enabled`; chat, workspace, memory, media,
+account, and agent APIs stayed public even with auth on.
+
+- `ApiAuthGuardMiddleware` denies every unauthenticated `/api/*` request when
+  `Auth:Enabled` is true, reading live configuration at request time (fail-closed, same
+  pattern as `SecureController`). Endpoints marked `[AllowAnonymous]` — health, models,
+  capabilities, plans — stay public for uptime probes and pricing surfaces.
+- `MapControllers().RequireAuthorization()` is additionally applied at builder time as
+  defense in depth when auth is configured.
+
+## 4. Monetization integrity — honor-system upgrade closed
+
+`POST /api/account/{email}/upgrade` previously let any anonymous client self-upgrade to a
+paid plan. Plan changes now require the `X-Auricrux-Billing-Key` header matching
+`Billing:UpgradeApiKey` (constant-time comparison). With no key configured, upgrades are
+disabled entirely — the key belongs to the payment webhook / back office, not clients.
+
+## 5. Durable state — restart-loss bugs closed
+
+- **FCA account links** moved from an in-memory dictionary to SQLite
+  (`Data/accounts/fca_links.db`) with write-through caching; links and unlinks survive
+  restarts.
+- **Star-rating feedback** moved from log-only to SQLite (`Data/memory/feedback.db`).
+
+## 6. Conversation-history correctness
+
+The client previously sent only *assistant* turns (newest-first) as conversation history,
+so models never saw the user's earlier questions. History is now proper chronological
+user/assistant pairs (last 6 turns) on both streaming and non-streaming paths.
+
+## 7. Security hardening
+
+- **CSP**: dropped `unsafe-eval` from `script-src` (Blazor Server does not need it); added
+  `object-src 'none'`, `base-uri 'self'`, `form-action 'self'`.
+- **Request body cap**: Kestrel `MaxRequestBodySize` set to 16 MB
+  (`RequestLimits:MaxBodyBytes`) so oversized uploads die at the transport.
+- **Dependencies**: `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite` 8.0.11 → 10.0.10; pinned
+  `SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3` 3.0.5 to clear the GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q (high) advisory.
+  `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` is clean across all projects.
+
+## Test coverage added
+
+| Area | Tests |
+|------|-------|
+| SSE streaming (`StreamingChatTests`) | content-type + delta/terminal-event contract, empty-query 400, freemium gating on stream, feedback on streamed interaction |
+| Auth gating (`AuthEnabledTests`) | chat/stream/workspace/memory 401 when auth on; health/models/capabilities/plans stay public |
+| Cloud gateway (`CloudModelGatewayTests`) | dark-until-keyed, prefix routing, five-provider resolution, Azure endpoint requirement, model-list override, `/api/models` surfacing |
+| Durability (`DurableStoresTests`) | FCA link save/unlink and feedback across simulated restarts |
+| Billing (`AuricruxApiIntegrationTests`) | upgrade denied without/with-wrong key; full upgrade flow with key |
+
+## Honest remaining gaps vs peers (unchanged by this pass)
+
+- `auricrux-fca` is still a system-prompt alias over a llama3.2-class base — the
+  checkpoint-70000 fine-tune export (AUX-017/018) remains the top model-quality gap.
+- Retrieval is keyword scoring over the 80-entry corpus, not embeddings/vector search.
+- No sandboxed code interpreter (deterministic construction calculator only).
+- Web browsing is operator-supplied-URL fetch, not autonomous search.
+- Video generation is storyboard/ffmpeg, not generative video.
